  "id": "gestalt-psychology",
  "term": "Gestalt psychology",
  "definition": "Gestalt psychology is an approach to perception that emphasizes how separate, similar parts can be mentally grouped and experienced as a larger whole. In this view, people often perceive an organized whole, or Gestalt, rather than only the individual elements that make it up.",
